{
 "_about": "What canon 0.36.0 accepted for the values `canon-0-37-option-forms` narrows (`atip.optionforms.13`): per option and value class, the commands whose argument stage (the value parser, the declared domain and the validators, which run before any state is read) took a value of that class. Measured on the released 0.36.0 binary (`canon 0.36.0`), one run per command and value on a copy of the story repository (`init` in a new git directory), a value counting as taken when the call was not refused with `--<option>` as its field (`init` names no field: `INIT_ARGUMENT_INVALID` counts as a refusal of `--providers`). `strategy approval-payload` and `strategy rollback` were run on a strategy id the repository does not hold, so only the argument stage was measured, not the later reads. `refused` lists the values 0.36.0 turned away already, so a class that 0.37 refuses and 0.36.0 refused too is not a row of the CHANGELOG. `atip.optionforms.13` holds the CHANGELOG to this file: every value of `accepted` that the build refuses now has a row. `canon-0-38-provider-option` re-baselined it in one way: the entries of `--providers`, which is not an option any more, are under `supersededBy038` and no longer read by `atip.optionforms.*`; the six other options are as they were.",
 "classes": {
  "date-only": "a date with no time (`2030-01-01`)",
  "leading-space": "white space before the value",
  "space-inside": "white space between the parts of a date",
  "one-digit-month": "a month of one digit (`2030-1-01`)",
  "one-digit-day": "a day of one digit (`2030-01-1`)",
  "signed-year": "a sign on the year (`+2030-01-01`)",
  "year-not-4-digits": "a year of fewer than four digits (`230-01-01`)",
  "space-separator": "a space for the `T` between the date and the time",
  "unicode-minus": "U+2212, the minus sign, for the `-` of an offset",
  "lowercase-t-z": "a lowercase `t` or `z` (RFC 3339 reads them: 0.37 still takes them)",
  "date-time": "a date-time spelled as RFC 3339 writes it (0.37 takes it)",
  "fraction": "a date-time with a fraction of a second (0.37 takes it)",
  "trailing-space": "white space after the value",
  "no-seconds": "a time without seconds (`10:00`)",
  "no-offset": "a time without an offset",
  "offset-without-colon": "an offset without its colon (`+0200`)"
 },
